        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-09-10T14:54:08Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think org.apache.http.legacy is also an optional library. Prior to its creation its classes were part of the bootclasspath, and then it was separated out into its own library. Just like android.test.base it is added to the classpath conditionally based on an App\u0027s target SDK version.\n\nandroid.test.mock is different. It was never part of the bootclasspath. However, it was part of the android.test.runner library and was separated out from there. It is automatically added to the classpath if \u0027android.test.runner\u0027 is being used.",
      "revId": "a00cb18d910f61a52370549321c557d0e498e80c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "286db766_914299a7",
        "filename": "dexpreopt/config.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 114,
      "author": {
        "id": 1550939
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-09-10T15:15:44Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Re org.apache.http.legacy, it sometimes appears with `required\u003dfalse` and sometimes with `required\u003dtrue` in the manifest (for both cases there are numerous occurrences). I can make it optional by default, but either way I have to add `optional_uses_libs` or `uses_libs` for the other half of the apps. Having a special case for optional and main case for required seemed more in-line with our previous discussion, but I can flip it.\n\nExample of required: https://source.corp.google.com/aosp-master/packages/apps/Settings/AndroidManifest.xml;l\u003d119\nExample of optional: https://source.corp.google.com/aosp-master/packages/apps/Gallery2/AndroidManifest.xml;l\u003d50",
      "parentUuid": "d1ea1522_e39cd5c0",
      "revId": "a00cb18d910f61a52370549321c557d0e498e80c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "b6913431_1a6dad84",
        "filename": "dexpreopt/config.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 114,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-09-10T15:33:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Those that mark it as required almost certainly has a target sdk version at or above the version in which the library was created. Conversely, those that mark it as optional will have a target sdk version below that.\n\nSo, its optional/required flag is dependent on target sdk version and that should probably be reflected in the handling of it here.",
      "parentUuid": "286db766_914299a7",
      "revId": "a00cb18d910f61a52370549321c557d0e498e80c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "dede05f2_28e6fdaf",
        "filename": "dexpreopt/config.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 114,
      "author": {
        "id": 1550939
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-09-10T16:44:58Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "There is conditional handling depending on target SDK version: https://source.corp.google.com/aosp-master/build/soong/dexpreopt/dexpreopt.go;l\u003d277-283\n\nBut the conditional logic is applied only in case org.apache.http.legacy is not either 1) present in `uses_libs`/`optional_uses_libs` in .bp file, or 2) added to `uses_libs` by Soong that computes transitional closure of SDK library dependencies.\n\nDexpreopt doesn\u0027t care about optional/required status, as long as the library is present at build time. The distinction is only when the library is missing: in that case missing optional library won\u0027t fail the build (and won\u0027t be added to dexpreopt).\n\nDo you mean that:\n\n1. We should not fail the build when org.apache.http.legacy is absent.\n\n2. We should always base the decision to add or not to add it to dexproept on target SDK version, no matter if it is in `uses_libs`/`optional_uses_libs` (whether from .bp file or added by Soong)?\n\nIn any case, can we decouple this change (which is a functional change) from the current CL, which fixes a different problem?",
      "parentUuid": "b6913431_1a6dad84",
      "revId": "a00cb18d910f61a52370549321c557d0e498e80c",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "1fea9eac_79012545",
        "filename": "dexpreopt/config.go",
        "patchSetId": 2
      },
      "lineNbr": 114,
      "author": {
        "id": 1039338
      },
      "writtenOn": "2020-09-10T18:58:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Neither. I was just pointing out that org.apache.http.legacy and android.test.base should be treated the same as they only differ by the version in which they were introduced. Everything you said about org.apache.http.legacy in terms of it being explicitly optional/required as well as implicitly optional applies to android.test.base too.\n\nI didn\u0027t realise that they were treated differently in the previous code so this didn\u0027t change that. In which case feel free to correct any differing treatment in a separate change.",
      "parentUuid": "dede05f2_28e6fdaf",
